  "text": "I shouldn't be saying this, but our front desk is the best magician in town. They make referrals disappear. Watch this. A GP sends us a patient, we leave one voicemail, and then poof, nobody ever calls back. Their best trick? Marking a case scheduled when nobody scheduled anything. The audience never even sees it. Here's the problem. Every disappearing act costs specialists tens of thousands in lost production every single month. So I checked tooth referrals analytics. It literally shows the leak. Received, contacted, scheduled, and where patients dropped off. It even tracks our ghost rate. Yes, that's a real number now. Very spooky, very fixable. Needs attention flags the cold cases. And anyone on the team can reassign them in one click. Now the math. One rescued referral pays for the system. One saved after staff turnover covers a whole year. When treatment is done, a signed completion note goes straight back to the GP. Happy GPs send more patients. Setup takes about five minutes. Check out tooth referral and retire your front desk's magic act for good.",
